<section class="how-does-it-work-section">
    <div>
        <h2>How to generate memes?</h2>

        <p class="how-does-it-work-text-content">
            <b>Just chat like you normally do or type /meme.</b>
            Once in a while Jstmemit picks a meme template, takes some GIFs, messages and mixes it all together using Markov
            chains algorithm (no LLMs!). Resulted meme is sent into your channel without you having to do anything.
        </p>

        <p class="how-does-it-work-text-content">
            By default Jstmemit is turned off in every channel and you have to manually select a channel where you want
            it to make memes by using /enable.
        </p>

        <img
            src="https://files.jstmemit.com/jstmemit/images/topgg/howDoesItWork.png"
            alt="illustration of how mixing separate messages into one meme text works"
        />
    </div>
</section>

<style>
    .how-does-it-work-section {
        background-color: var(--color-ash-black);
        display: flex;
        justify-content: center;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 1rem;
        position: relative;
        padding: 3.5rem 2rem 2rem;
        border-radius: 2rem;
        margin-top: 5.5rem;
        border: 2px solid var(--color-bubblegum-pink);
    }

    .how-does-it-work-section img {
        width: 100%;
        margin-left: 1rem;
        padding-bottom: 1rem;
    }
</style>
